  "id": "DrugBank_DB15404 - MONDO_809",
  "verbalization": "Heparin, Bovine is associated with Purpura Fulminans through a series of indications that suggest a potential role in the pathophysiology of the condition. The evidence indicates that Heparin, Bovine is linked to Acquired Purpura Fulminans, which in turn is associated with both Dalteparin and Parnaparin, all of which are linked to Purpura Fulminans. This suggests a possible pathway where Heparin, Bovine may exert a therapeutic or pathophysiological effect that is indirectly linked to the development of Purpura Fulminans through the use of related anticoagulants. The presence of multiple indications pointing to Purpura Fulminans, along with the shared association between Heparin, Bovine and Dalteparin, implies a possible mechanism involving anticoagulant activity or a related pathophysiological process. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Heparin, Bovine to be involved in the development of Purpura Fulminans through its interaction with anticoagulant agents, though further investigation is needed to clarify the exact mechanism.",
